\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces CT saturation sweep results (post-fix). Bars: external FPR (Conv blue, \textsc {sambp}{} red — both zero after fix). Lines: internal TPR (Conv blue, \textsc {sambp}{} red dashed). The conventional relay's external FPR rises at $\varepsilon _{\rm CT}= 0.05$; \textsc {sambp}{} holds FPR~=~0.000 across the full range while maintaining TPR~=~1.000.}}{6}{figure.caption.8}%
